In nethack, it's not speed which kills, but lack of speed.  
Being burdened drastically reduces your and increases your 
opponent's relative speed.  

> Will I always be burdened...just based on the armour I where
> to protect myself?  

Three strategies to reduce weight: 

1)  Build up strength.  A highly welcome side-effect of Sokoban 
is that all this boulder-pushing should increase low 
strength at least one or two points.  Some activities, 
like kicking in doors, are also beneficial for building 
up strength.  The supreme way of getting strength, however, 
is the choice of a good diet and of the correct equipment 
(if you want to get spoiled, have a look at food, potions 
and armour spoilers).  

2)  Choose armor with good protection/weight ratio.  Mithril 
is famous for being light yet hard, while, say, orcish 
chain mail is rather heavy and of inferior quality.  I'd 
sacrifice one or even two points of AC if that gives me 
an armour I can wear at ease.  

3)  Don't be a pack-rat.  Start to make stashes of loot early 
on.  Chests are a good place to hide loot.  There are ways 
of protecting the loot further agains possible misfortunes, 
but I don't know how spoiled you want to become.  

> A bag of holding can only do so much.

Many items' usefulness can be enhanced by proper treatment.  

